# flyctl launch added from .gitignore
# Environment — never commit real credentials
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
**/sdk/node/node_modules

# Build output
**/dist
**/sdk/node/dist

# macOS
**/.DS_Store

# Logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
fly.toml

# Ignored by git and, until now, not by Docker: 17MB of screenshots, reference
# material and tool state that was uploaded to the remote builder on every
# deploy. None of it reaches the running image, because the runtime stage takes
# only /app/dist, but all of it was in the build context. Keeping the two
# ignore files aligned is also what stops a file git cannot see from riding
# into a build that the commit marker then claims to describe.
**/scripts/shots-out
**/.reference
**/.hallmark
**/.claude
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
